                <pb facs="0667" n="587" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg587"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell reports that the situation at Port au Prince is extremely
                    interesting, it being reported that the President will probably leave on May 12,
                    in which event bloodshed is feared; that the south demands the Presidency; that
                    Firmin and Leconte are candidates from the north.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
